From: u99a06696c483481a at groups.google.com (Edward Rigdon)
Date: Sun, 03 Jan 2021 15:50:19 +0000
Subject: Re: Lavaan Warning during CFA Analysis with Ordinal Data (vcov does not appear to be positive definite)
Message-ID: <kj80otxmnkk.qLIFkDy8BwAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <kj80otxmnkk.HE2UvMizBwAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
References: <kj80otxmnkk.x4wIJBuABwAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com> <kj80otxmnkk.HE2UvMizBwAJ@lavaan.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/lavaan/c/kj80otxmnkk/m/qLIFkDy8BwAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With ordinal variables, the set of parameters includes thresholds related parameters. With skewed data, there may be high uncertainty about these additional parameters, perhaps making identification marginal. You might try simulating a much larger dataset to see if sample size might be the problem.

On Sat, Jan 2, 2021 at 5:07 PM Patrick (Malone Quantitative) <mal...@malonequantitative.com> wrote:

> Erdem,
>
> Nothing jumps out at me. I suspect it reflects the fact that some of your factors are so highly correlated.
>
> Pat
>
> On Sat, Jan 2, 2021 at 4:28 PM Erdem Uygun <uygun...@gmail.com> wrote:
