I am still learning SEM, what I understand two-step SEM method according to Anderson and Gerbing (1988) is:  first I need to specify and tested the measurement model, then review the model fitting related parameter to tweak the measurement model. Then I need to specify and tested the full model, last is the trimmed model after removing the non-significant paths.
My proposed casual model is:
So first:
STEP1:
measurement_model<-
  '
#measurement model
A=~a1
B=~b1+b2
C=~c1+c2+c3+c4
D=~d1+d2
    '
fit <- cfa(model = measurement_model, data = data)

STEP2:
full_sem_model<-
  '
#measurement model
A=~a1
B=~b1+b2
C=~c1+c2+c3+c4
D=~d1+d2
    '
#regressions
A~B+Age
B~Gender + Age + A
C~A+Age
............(this is just example)
```
fit <- sem(model = full_sem_model, data = data)

STEP 3
Trimmed model

Above is the basic steps according to my understanding, are my steps correct? Please correct me if my understanding is wrong.

Thank you

